{"title":"Cardiac Surgery Technologist Roadmap","role":"Cardiac Surgery Technologist","summary":"A Cardiac Surgery Technologist working in a Perfusion Technology pathway supports cardiac and cardiothoracic surgical teams, particularly in procedures requiring extracorporeal circulation and advanced cardiovascular equipment.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Perfusion Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Cardiac Surgery Technologist working in a Perfusion Technology pathway supports cardiac and cardiothoracic surgical teams, particularly in procedures requiring extracorporeal circulation and advanced cardiovascular equipment."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on training, institutional scope, and applicable regulations, the role can involve working closely with cardiac surgeons, cardiac anaesthesiologists, perfusionists, nurses, and operating-theatre teams."},{"type":"p","text":"Key areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) support"},{"text":"Heart-lung machine preparation"},{"text":"Extracorporeal circulation equipment"},{"text":"Cardiopulmonary bypass circuits"},{"text":"Blood conservation systems"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Cardiac surgery equipment"},{"text":"Perfusion-related documentation"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Infection control and equipment safety"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Scope note","text":"Perfusion practice is a specialized clinical function. The exact responsibilities of a cardiac surgery technologist, perfusion technologist, and perfusionist differ by qualification, hospital, jurisdiction, and applicable professional regulations. A graduate should not independently operate extracorporeal-support systems without the required clinical training and authorization."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":